689..762 Comment "/// Marks on a computation, flushed at the end. Where writes go nowhere a"
763..839 Comment "/// flushed mark leaves nothing, and where the state is kept flushing a mark"
840..914 Comment "/// keeps it. The two overlap at `flush(mark(k))` in the rows holding both"
915..990 Comment "/// `State` and `Sink`; there marks and flushes are erased, so both reducts"
991..1005 Comment "/// reach `k`."
